kunzite: Adreno 710, glue plan K4 (main repo ios/gpu-glue-plan.md 3.3, 4): parameters, and
RedwoodGPU published. redwood_gpu_parameter answers MSM_PARAM_* as Linux's adreno_get_param does,
with glue plan 3.3's values: GPU_ID 710, GMEM_SIZE 0x80000, CHIP_ID 0x07010000 (FDT qcom,chipid),
MAX_FREQ 345 MHz (the level held), TIMESTAMP the GMU's always-on counter (19.2 MHz; kgsl gen7 reads
that one), GMEM_BASE 0x1000000 (kgsl's uche_gmem_base), PRIORITIES 1,
PP_PGTABLE/FAULTS/SUSPENDS/RAYTRACING 0, HIGHEST_BANK_BIT 14 (LPDDR4X), UBWC_SWIZZLE 6,
MACROTILE_MODE 1 (RBBM_NC_MODE_CNTL 1, boot #48); VA_START/VA_SIZE stay unanswered (the kernel hands
out addresses). Keep mode calls RedwoodGPUStart() once the GPU is kept and submission is set up: the
RedwoodGPU service (msm DRM selectors 0x40-0x4c, 0x7e) is registered for userland. When the kept GPU
goes, RedwoodGPUStop() first (RedwoodGPU's lock taken, so no client is in the middle of a request;
redwood_gpu_stop makes the GPU not ready), then the last fence, then the undo. Log lines under 256
bytes (the console cuts there and drops the newline, boot #50): the keep report is three lines (now
with the number of free GPU address ranges), the run's opening step list two, redwood_gpu_report's
first line two. Test: kgpu=24 kgpu_keep=1 kgpu_keep_s=600, then userland/gpu/redwood-check (built on
the Mac, put in /tmp and run over the agent) reads the parameters and makes, maps, writes, reads
back and frees a buffer.

